@@ -63,6 +63,16 @@ A load and a prepare-only job share this one preparation (device selection, plan
 device and preparing programs with the kernel cache), so both produce and look up identical tuning
 keys; the prepare-only job ends there, while a load continues with state planning, graph sealing,
 resource allocation, weight import and warm-up.
+CUDA projection launch geometry owns the row tile and pipeline depth. Its grid
+covers every submitted row and its declared shared bound includes staged activations,
+code chunks, both coefficient-record buffers and decoded warp coefficients. A
+single-stage candidate synchronizes every consuming warp before tile reuse, then
+waits for loads and a block barrier before multiplication. It preserves the k order,
+F32 accumulation and epilogue rounding of the multistage candidates. A 32-row
+single-stage default fits the Pascal shared-memory floor for every admitted weight
+representation; larger multistage candidates remain subject to the opened device's
+actual limits. Tile choices never select a model family or change stored weights.
+
 Native entries with declared tuning parameters are tuned on the opened device during this
 preparation, on the first preparation for each tuning key, whether by a load or by the prepare-only
 job that follows a catalog installation: each such entry registers a tuning case
